{"builder":"Make one pull request that meets every one of these acceptance lines:\n- math.js exports clamp(x, lo, hi), which returns x limited to the range lo to hi\n- clamp(x, lo, hi) throws a RangeError when lo is greater than hi\n- README.md documents every function math.js exports\n- npm test passes\n\nRepository facts: math.js is CommonJS and currently ends with `module.exports = { add, subtract, multiply };`. Tests live in test/math.test.js and run with `npm test` (which is `node --test`). README.md has an `## API` section with `### add(a, b)` and `### multiply(a, b)` headings; it has NO entry for `subtract`, so the third line fails today until you add one.\n\nSteps:\n1. In math.js add a function `clamp(x, lo, hi)` with a short doc comment in the same style as the others. If `lo > hi`, throw `new RangeError(...)` with a clear message. Otherwise return `lo` when `x < lo`, `hi` when `x > hi`, else `x` (so clamp(-5, 0, 100) is 0, clamp(140, 0, 100) is 100, clamp(5, 0, 10) is 5, and lo === hi is allowed). Add `clamp` to `module.exports`, keeping add, subtract and multiply exported.\n2. In README.md, under `## API`, add a `### subtract(a, b)` section (returns `a` minus `b`, with a small example) and a `### clamp(x, lo, hi)` section that says it returns `x` limited to the range `lo` to `hi` and throws a `RangeError` when `lo` is greater than `hi`, with an example such as clamp(140, 0, 100) // 100. Keep the existing heading style `### name(args)` so each exported function has its own heading.\n3. In test/math.test.js, import clamp and add tests: values below, inside and above the range, the boundaries, lo === hi, negative ranges, and `assert.throws(() => clamp(5, 10, 0), RangeError)`.\n4. Run `npm test` and confirm it exits 0 with no failing tests before opening the pull request.","verifier":"At the PR head, from the repository root, run each check below in order. Each check maps to one acceptance line.\n\nCheck 1 — expect line: \"math.js exports clamp(x, lo, hi), which returns x limited to the range lo to hi\"\nRun:\nnode -e \"const m=require('./math.js');const c=m.clamp;if(typeof c!=='function'){console.log('FAIL: clamp not exported');process.exit(1)}const cases=[[5,0,10,5],[-5,0,100,0],[140,0,100,100],[0,0,100,0],[100,0,100,100],[3,3,3,3],[-7,-10,-2,-7],[-20,-10,-2,-10]];let bad=0;for(const [x,lo,hi,want] of cases){const got=c(x,lo,hi);if(got!==want){bad++;console.log('FAIL clamp('+x+','+lo+','+hi+') = '+got+', want '+want)}}console.log(bad?'FAIL':'PASS');process.exit(bad?1:0)\"\nPASS: prints PASS and exits 0 (clamp is an exported function and every case returns x limited to [lo, hi]).\nFAIL: prints any FAIL line or exits non-zero, or the command throws.\n\nCheck 2 — expect line: \"clamp(x, lo, hi) throws a RangeError when lo is greater than hi\"\nRun:\nnode -e \"const c=require('./math.js').clamp;if(typeof c!=='function'){console.log('FAIL: clamp not exported');process.exit(1)}let bad=0;for(const [x,lo,hi] of [[5,10,0],[0,1,0],[50,100,-100]]){try{c(x,lo,hi);bad++;console.log('FAIL: no throw for clamp('+x+','+lo+','+hi+')')}catch(e){if(!(e instanceof RangeError)){bad++;console.log('FAIL: clamp('+x+','+lo+','+hi+') threw '+(e&&e.name)+', not RangeError')}}}console.log(bad?'FAIL':'PASS');process.exit(bad?1:0)\"\nPASS: prints PASS and exits 0 (each call with lo > hi throws a RangeError).\nFAIL: prints any FAIL line or exits non-zero.\n\nCheck 3 — expect line: \"README.md documents every function math.js exports\"\nRun:\nnode -e \"const fs=require('fs');const m=require('./math.js');const readme=fs.readFileSync('README.md','utf8');const names=Object.keys(m).filter(k=>typeof m[k]==='function');let bad=0;for(const n of names){if(!new RegExp('^#+ .*\\\\b'+n+'\\\\s*\\\\(','m').test(readme)){bad++;console.log('FAIL: README.md has no heading documenting '+n+'()')}}console.log('exports: '+names.join(', '));console.log(bad?'FAIL':'PASS');process.exit(bad?1:0)\"\nThen open README.md and confirm that each name in the printed `exports:` list has a section with a description of what it does (not just a bare heading).\nPASS: the command prints PASS and exits 0, and every exported function listed has a describing section in README.md.\nFAIL: the command prints a FAIL line or exits non-zero, or any exported function's section lacks a description. (Note: before the change, subtract is undocumented, so this check fails at the base.)\n\nCheck 4 — expect line: \"npm test passes\"\nRun:\nnpm test; echo \"exit $?\"\nPASS: the last line is `exit 0` and the TAP summary shows `# fail 0`.\nFAIL: any non-zero exit or any failing test.\n\nAdvisory (not part of PASS/FAIL):\n- Check that test/math.test.js includes tests for clamp, including a RangeError case.\n- Check that add, subtract and multiply are still exported and unchanged."}